A sacrifice on the altar would be killing something that's alive as
part of the ritual.  The offering (a burnt offering, here) is a
different tradition.  Offerings traditionally include animals, food,
wine, gold, just about anything that has some value - it doesn't have
to be alive, and I would argue that it's unlikely that wine or gold
has a soul.  In addition, the animals are already dead, so unless the
souls are trapped inside the dead bodies, you're not offering the
soul.  It's showing the god that you still remember exactly who you're
working for.  Or, "It's the thought that counts."

Stormbringer is another matter.... "Souls!  Souls, for my Lord Arioch!"
